cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "llm-se-bench: an execution-based benchmark harness for LLMs on Java software-engineering tasks"
message: "If you use this software or its task data, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Gia Bach"
    family-names: "Vo"
    email: "hung072912@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bachcodingg/LLM-SE-bench"
abstract: >-
  llm-se-bench evaluates large language models on Java code generation, bug
  fixing and God Class refactoring inside a deterministic Docker sandbox.
  It records per-call cost and latency for every API call, extracts
  Chidamber-Kemerer design metrics from generated code, and runs
  non-parametric significance tests over the resulting outcomes. The
  published run covers 58 tasks across four datasets and three frontier
  models, 522 evaluations in total.
keywords:
  - "large language models"
  - "benchmark"
  - "software engineering"
  - "code generation"
  - "program repair"
  - "refactoring"
  - "java"
  - "ck metrics"
  - "cost accounting"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-18"
